From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: report charge_now and charge_full

The PM8150B fuel gauge reports capacity (%) and current_now but neither
charge_now nor energy_now, so userspace that works out the time left
from charge / current (MangoHud, UPower) shows 0. Report charge_now as
capacity x charge_full_design and charge_full as the design capacity
(the gauge doesn't learn the battery's real capacity).
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -861,6 +861,8 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MIN_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MAX_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP_MIN,
@@ -935,6 +937,16 @@
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
 		val->intval = chip->batt_info->charge_full_design_uah;
 		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL:
+		/* The gauge doesn't learn capacity: report the design value */
+		val->intval = chip->batt_info->charge_full_design_uah;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW:
+		ret = chip->ops->get_capacity(chip, &temp);
+		if (ret)
+			break;
+		val->intval = chip->batt_info->charge_full_design_uah / 100 * temp;
+		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
 		val->intval = 1;
 		break;
